- op: discuss  # 6171
  at: '2026-08-21T06:31:45Z'  # 6171
  by: agent  # 6171
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 6171
  clock: 3  # 6171
  nonce: '6171'  # 6171
  message: "CLOSED. Shipped a0f6336afc (PR #455). Behavioral evidence on the MERGED tree, at the stage the defect lives -- taint runs only inside cmd_verify_claims, so a unit-level assertion would not have been closure evidence.\n\nLIVE TWO-ARM REPRO, merged dev, production CLI, two fixtures differing ONLY in whether the tainted value is passed as an argument:\n\n  data = sys.stdin.read()\n  tempfile.TemporaryDirectory()      -> untrusted-input-no-host-fs CLEAN, exit 0\n                                        \"No unsanitized untrusted_input data reaches host_fs zone\"\n  tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(data)  -> untrusted-input-no-host-fs VIOLATED, exit 1\n\nThat is the whole invariant in two lines: the sink, the source and the reachability are identical across the arms; only the argument list differs.\n\nCORPUS RESULT (same delta design as measurement 0003 -- baseline clone at 148fae52b3, isolated XDG_CACHE_HOME per arm, instrument held constant): of the 35 flows the construction-edge widening added across mitmproxy/poetry/pretix, 29 are removed and 6 survive. Marginal precision 2.9% -> 16.7%. Five PRE-EXISTING false positives go too, and readfile.py is the clean illustration -- line 56 logging.error(\"Flow file corrupted.\") is silenced while line 67 logging.error(f\"Cannot load flows: {e}\") four lines below still flows, because an f-string is ast.JoinedStr and not a constant.\n\nTHE ACCEPTANCE CRITERION THIS ITEM WAS FILED WITH HOLDS: the 0003 true positive SURVIVES. mitmproxy magisk -> write_magisk_module -> ZipFile(path,\"w\") is present in the fixed arm. That was filed precisely because a fix that removed both the FPs and the TP would have looked like success on FP count alone.\n\nTHE RECEIVER HALF WAS FOUND BY MEASUREMENT, NOT REVIEW, and it is the part worth remembering. An argument-only first cut stamped pretix Path(DATA_DIR).mkdir(parents=False, exist_ok=True) -- both arguments literal, while DATA_DIR is an environment read and the receiver decides WHICH DIRECTORY IS CREATED. It silenced 9 real findings (6 mkdir in pretix, f.write and three logger.warn in mitmproxy) and no amount of reading the diff caught it; running the corpus did. Two shapes are now accepted: a bare-name call (no receiver at all) and module.attr() where the receiver is a known imported module.\n\nSTRUCTURE, one home per fact: axis_meta_keys declares the key; py.py stamps ONCE over the slice of edges each call appended (all fourteen Edge.create sites and any added later); ir.py merges conservatively across collapsed call sites because deduplicate_edges keeps the FIRST edge and an arrival-order-decided marker would silence a real flow on the strength of a different call site; taint.py gates BOTH propagation arms through one predicate.\n\nNOT CLAIMED, and each is a real limit rather than a hedge: the producer is PYTHON-ONLY, so the gate is inert on go/js until their analyzers stamp -- sound, because absence means \"cannot prove\", but the precision win does not generalize yet. Five false positives survive, from the two mechanisms 0003 named separately (co-location-file, and ZipFile taking a real but untainted argument); neither is closed by this. And -1 parses as ast.UnaryOp so TemporaryFile(\"w\", -1) stays unstamped -- pinned by a test as a deliberate conservative gap, a missed precision win that can never silence a finding."  # 6171
